<http://data.silknow.org/event/dd028137-8e47-39df-b131-6175187a8a2e>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This cloth acquired by the East India Company Museum in 1855 probably came from the Paris International Exhibition of that year. The label gives the name of the cloth in contemporary spelling and and carries the name of the craftsman:\n\" KAMSHAB JUNGA LAH\nMINAKAR\"  by BUDHU\nTransferred from the India Museum in 1879. 1880 Register Entry:  [ROOM 8. Case 60.]  '0827. \"KINCOB.\" Piece of, red ground, gold and coloured design with inscription; Benares. 3,245'"@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6c4233d5-d6cd-3fdb-806b-1e75934b3569> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This cloth acquired by the East India Company Museum in 1855 probably came from the Paris International Exhibition of that year. The label gives the name of the cloth in contemporary spelling and and carries the name of the craftsman:\n\" KAMSHAB JUNGA LAH\nMINAKAR\"  by BUDHU\nTransferred from the India Museum in 1879. 1880 Register Entry:  [ROOM 8. Case 60.]  '0827. \"KINCOB.\" Piece of, red ground, gold and coloured design with inscription; Benares. 3,245'"@en .

<https://sws.geonames.org/1253405/>
